# Shop Desk — Cypress tests (JavaScript)

_Generated by StepForge — by Md Zarin Tasnim on 2026-10-07 from the **Staging** environment._

3 scenarios: Checkout with every UI step, Orders API, Data and email.

## Setup

```bash
npm install
cp .env.example .env   # then fill in the values
```

## Run

```bash
npx cypress run    # headless, JUnit results in results/
npx cypress open   # interactive
```

## Configuration

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `BASE_URL` | Staging environment (default `https://staging.shop.test`) |
| `API_VERSION` | {{env.api-version}} (default `v2`) |
| `REGION` | {{env.region}} (default `eu`) |
| `ADMIN_PASSWORD` | secret {{secret.adminPassword}} — never commit its value |
| `API_TOKEN` | secret {{secret.apiToken}} — never commit its value |
| `DB_MAIN_URL` | "main" database (pg), e.g. postgres://user:password@localhost:5432/db |
| `DB_LOCAL_URL` | "local" database (sqlite), e.g. sqlite:./app.db |
| `DB_UNKNOWN_URL` | "unknown" database, e.g. postgres://…, mysql://… or sqlite:./app.db |
| `MAILPIT_URL` | Mailpit web/API address (default `http://127.0.0.1:8025`) |

Secret values are not part of the export: set them in `.env` locally and as CI secrets in pipelines.

## Layout

- `cypress/e2e/` — one spec per scenario, grouped by module; one test per test case
- `cypress/pages/` — page objects (one function per element)
- `cypress/support/` — configuration, helpers, the `fill` command and Testing Library queries
- `cypress/plugins/` — Node tasks for the database and Mailpit
- `sql/` — the SQL of each database step

## Notes

- Elements are found with Testing Library (`findByRole`, `findByLabelText`, …), which match StepForge's role, label and text locators.
- Steps that use values from earlier steps run inside `cy.then()` so they read the value when the step runs.
- Cypress runs in one tab and needs plugins for iframes and drag and drop; such steps are marked `TODO(StepForge)`.
- Exported on 2026-10-07; re-export from StepForge after changing the scenarios.

